============================================================
REQUIREMENTS FOR request.js
============================================================

### CORE ARCHITECTURE
- Must use native fetch() (NOT axios)
- Must include:
  - BASE_URL injection (support Vite + Webpack + Node)
  - unified request wrapper
  - timeout wrapper (configurable)
  - retry mechanism for network errors
  - request interceptor (token injection)
  - response interceptor (JSON + text auto parsing)
  - unified error normalization
  - convenience methods: GET / POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE

### TOKEN HANDLING
- Token must be inserted automatically into Authorization: Bearer <token>
- Token must be obtained via a pluggable function:
    function getToken() { ... }
- Do NOT hardcode login logic

### ERROR HANDLING
- Must wrap HTTP errors into a consistent object:
    error.status
    error.data
    error.message
- Must throw on:
    - non-2xx responses
    - network failures
    - timeout

### TIMEOUT SUPPORT
- Implement timeout by wrapping fetch with Promise.race
- Default timeout: 15000ms

### RETRY SUPPORT
- Automatic retry for:
    - RequestTimeout
    - network failure
- retry limit = 1

### REQUEST HELPERS
Implement:
    request.get(url, params?, config?)
    request.post(url, body?, config?)
    request.put(url, body?, config?)
    request.patch(url, body?, config?)
    request.delete(url, body?, config?)

### FORM DATA SUPPORT
- If body is FormData → DO NOT set Content-Type
- Otherwise set Content-Type: application/json

### CODE STYLE
- Single file output: request.js
- No TypeScript
- ES module syntax (export default request)

